From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 14:15:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04492/11362] [outer-loop] Push the lp85 cell-recall lever:
 coverage gives a modest +0.063, gap NOT closed (mechanic OOD)

Operator-directed ("both", Task 2). lp85 is the worst change-LOCATION transferer (0.278)
but has the MOST data (418 transitions) -> not data-starved. Tested both levers:

  AXIS A (more lp85 fewshot adaptation, saved 20-game prior): plateaus -- fs40 0.250,
    fs80 0.278, fs160 0.309, fs240 0.293 (warm beats scratch throughout, but below the
    +0.05 bar). NOT an adaptation-data problem.
  AXIS B (broader corpus: retrain prior on 24 games incl the other holdouts): 0.278 ->
    0.341 (+0.063). Coverage helps, modestly.

VERDICT: modestly pushed via coverage, but the gap is NOT closed -- 0.341 stays far below
the well-transferring ka59/sc25/tn36 band (0.75-0.89). lp85's mechanic is substantially
OOD for the cross-game prior; the real fix is a representation/corpus-diversity change
(lp85-like mechanics in training), not more of the same data. NOTE (per the Task-1
corrigendum): cell-recall is change-LOCATION only; exact transition VALUES remain ~0 --
this lever serves probe-efficiency, not world-modeling. missing-verifier gap logged in
the artifact (lp85 hidden-state-dependent change-VALUE prediction). adversarial_verify clean.

